  "description": "A curious and sure-footed wanderer, happiest roaming beyond the map and carrying everything needed to turn distant horizons into home. Flatmount 160 makes for a strong and precise design when working with steel. Adapts to either 160 or 180 rotors with typical post mount brakes. 3D-printed frame junctions unlocks a level of design freedom that allows complex shapes, tyre clearances, and cable routing solutions that would be impossible achieve with traditional steel fabrication methods. UDH and direct mount derailleur options all work. Additionally there are M5 rack mounts on both dropouts. Optimised heal clerance. As well as two 750ml bottle mounts inside the front triangle there is an additional third mount under the downtube for either another bottle or cargo cage. Each frame gets its own number printed into the frame. Right here in Ōtautahi, Christchurch. 2.4” tyres fit with ease with room left over for that peanut butter mud.. The unique curved seat tube and chainstay yoke mean that mud also has less area to build up like conventional designs do. Headtubes, bottom braket shells and seat tube collars are all custom Süfur designs and are machined just 26km from Süfur HQ. A custom Elite tubeset produced by Velospec. Designed, tested and fabricated all in-house.",
